# Content file type tags

**Language:** English.

Use this when a screen shows downloadable content file types as tags (Drawings column, file pickers, tooltips).

**Figma:** Part Search – RSFC, frame **Content file type tags** (`11341:6250`). Component is DS `Tag__Colorful` with **border on**. Source list: [Content File Types](https://ooden.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Hydra/pages/1751580673/Content+File+Types).

## Color by file type

Map the label to an existing `HydraColorfulTag` preset. Do not invent hex colors. `Tag__Colorful` has no `red` variant, so DWG uses `orange`.

| File type | Preset | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| RFA | `blue` | Revit family. Primary BIM file. |
| STEP | `geekblue` | Neutral 3D solid. |
| PDF | `cyan` | Dimensioned reference drawing. |
| DWG | `orange` | AutoCAD drawing. |
| IGES | `magenta` | Neutral geometry exchange. |
| SAT | `purple` | ACIS solid exchange. |
| IEZ | `green` | Fabrication CAD MEP package. |
| TXT | `gold` | Revit support file. Bundled with RFA, not a standalone download. |
| PNG | `lime` | Preview image. Not a modeling file. |

Code: `CONTENT_FILE_TYPE_TAG_PRESET` in `src/search/contentFileTypeTags.ts`. An unknown type uses the default `HydraTag`, not a new color.

**One color per type, everywhere.** This table is the only mapping, in every screen of the repo and every frame in Figma. Never give a file type a different color on another screen (for example a purple PDF or a volcano DWG). In code, always render file-type tags through `ContentFileTypeTags` or `contentFileTypeTagPreset`, never with a hand-picked `preset`. In Figma, the `Tag__Colorful` `color` variant must follow this table, and the layer name must match the title (`Tag__Colorful / PDF`).

Keep the same preset everywhere that type appears as a tag.

## Drawings column

- Spec columns (pipe size, coating, material, and the rest) are **plain text**. Do not color those cells with tags.
- Show at most **three** file-type tags (`CONTENT_FILE_TYPE_TAG_VISIBLE_COUNT`).
- When a variant has more than three types, add a neutral `+X` tag (DS `Tag`, `type=default, border=true`). `X` is the hidden count.
- Hovering `+X` (hover only, no click) opens an antd **Tooltip** with a light background that shows the hidden types as the same colored tags. Code: `<Tooltip color={token.colorBgElevated} placement="top" title={tags}>` with the tags in a `Flex gap={token.marginXS}`. Antd Tooltip `title` accepts any content.
- Figma: DS `Tooltip` `placement=top`, `show arrow` on, `show title` off, `show content` on, with `Tag__Colorful` instances in the `content` slot. Override the tooltip and arrow fill with `Color/Neutral/Background/colorBgElevated` (this matches antd `color`).
- Do not use `Popover` for this, and do not list the hidden types as plain text.
- In Figma the DS `Table / Table cell` holds one tag only. The Drawings cell is a local auto-layout frame named `Drawings cell` that copies the cell's padding, gap, fill, and bottom border variables. It contains `Tag__Colorful` and `Tag` instances. Do not detach the table cell.
- Keep the Drawings column wide enough for three tags plus `+X` on one line (`token.sizeUnit * 64` in the variant selection modal).
- The expanded row panel repeats the same tags after a `Documents:` label (Base/Normal, `colorTextDescription`). Same preset colors, same three-plus-`+X` limit. In Figma this is a local frame named `Documents` inside the panel's `Meta` row.
- Order follows the variant’s `drawingFileTypes` list. Do not regroup 3D exchange types.

## Do not

- Do not add tag colors, tokens, or a new Tag component for this.
- Do not use one color for every file type.
- Do not show TXT as its own download choice. It stays bundled with RFA.
